/**
@defgroup core Core
@brief Application services and coordinate types.
*/
/**
@namespace TigerEngine::Key
@ingroup core
@brief Named keyboard codes matching GLFW, independent of GLFW headers.
A-Z are letters; D0-D9 are the number row; KP0-KP9 are keypad digits.
Function keys F1-F25, editing/navigation keys, punctuation and left/right
modifiers are available. Unknown is a sentinel and polls as false.
Use these with Input::IsKeyPressed; they represent held key state, not text input.
*/
/**
@namespace TigerEngine::Mouse
@ingroup core
@brief Mouse button codes for Input::IsMouseButtonPressed.
Button1-Button8 map to GLFW buttons. ButtonLeft, ButtonRight and ButtonMiddle
alias Button1, Button2 and Button3 respectively.
*/
/**
@defgroup scene Scene and behavior
@brief Objects, components, animation and basic collision.
*/
/**
@defgroup graphics Graphics
@brief Rendering, materials, textures, shaders and cameras.
*/
/**
@defgroup ui User interface
@brief Debug controls and screen-space game UI.
*/

/**
@class TigerEngine::Application
@ingroup core
@brief Owns the window, engine systems, current scene and game UI.
Construct before loading GPU resources. Only one instance may be active.
Construction throws if window/graphics initialization fails. Run enters the
frame loop; destruction releases scene/UI GPU resources before closing the window.
TimeScale multiplies scene delta time. SetTargetFPS with a positive value disables
VSync; SetVSync(true) can re-enable it. UI is still processed at TimeScale zero.
@see TigerEngine::Scene, TigerEngine::UIManager
*/
/**
@fn void TigerEngine::Application::Run()
@brief Starts the scene and processes frames until close or Escape.
Updates objects, draws the world and UI, presents the frame and polls events.
Frame-loop exceptions are caught and logged by the current implementation.
*/
/**
@fn void TigerEngine::Application::Close()
@brief Requests a normal exit from the application loop after the current frame.
Window/context and engine resources are released by Application destruction.
*/
/**
@fn TigerEngine::Point2D TigerEngine::Application::GetFramebufferSize() const
@brief Returns the window drawing area's width/height in framebuffer pixels.
Initialized during startup and updated by the framebuffer resize callback.
These are not logical window coordinates; values can differ on high DPI displays.
The value can be zero while minimized. Reading it does not query OpenGL.
*/
/**
@fn float TigerEngine::Application::GetAspectRatio() const
@brief Returns framebuffer width divided by height, or 1 when height is zero.
Uses the same cached dimensions as GetFramebufferSize.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Input
@ingroup core
@brief Polls keyboard/mouse state and converts cursor coordinates.
Key/button queries return true while held. ImGui capture suppresses matching
gameplay queries. Pixel positions use logical window pixels with top-left origin;
NDC uses center origin and upward Y. World positions use the active camera matrix.
No window means false/zero results. Minimized-window conversion returns zero.
*/
/**
@fn TigerEngine::Point2D TigerEngine::Input::ScreenToWorld(Point2D point, Point2D windowSize, const OrthographicCamera& camera)
@brief Converts logical window pixels to camera/world coordinates.
@param point Cursor or other point in top-left-origin logical pixels.
@param windowSize Logical window width/height, not framebuffer size.
@param camera Camera whose view/projection defines the world.
@return World point, or (0,0) for nonpositive/nonfinite dimensions.
*/
/**
@typedef TigerEngine::Point2D
@ingroup core
@brief Floating-point x/y coordinates, implemented as glm::vec2.
The API determines whether values are pixels, normalized coordinates or world units.
Vector2 is an alias of the same type.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::AssetPath
@ingroup core
@brief Resolves asset names against a configurable asset folder.
The default root is assets beside the executable. Both image.png and
assets/image.png address that root. Absolute paths are used directly. Resolve
normalizes paths, including missing files, and rejects an empty path. SetRoot
before Application construction or resource loading to use a different folder.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::AssetManager
@ingroup core
@brief Caches shared textures and fonts by normalized absolute paths.
LoadTexture and LoadFont require an active OpenGL context on the render thread.
Fonts additionally use pixel height as a cache key. Load failures throw and are
not cached. Unload/Clear remove only cache references; retained shared handles
stay valid. A reload after eviction may allocate another copy of the resource.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::AudioSystem
@ingroup core
@brief Plays sound effects and a single music stream through miniaudio.
Application initializes and shuts down this system. Paths use AssetPath.
PlaySound2D is fire-and-forget; PlayMusic replaces the previous music stream.
Global volume affects the full mix; music volume affects that stream separately.
Initialization/playback errors are logged. Audio is not cached by AssetManager.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Scene
@ingroup scene
@brief Owns objects and dispatches their lifecycle and rendering calls.
AddObject transfers unique ownership. GetObjects returns a snapshot of borrowed
pointers. The active camera pointer is borrowed and must remain valid and nonnull.
Clear destroys objects and restores the default camera; call it outside iteration.
Current mouse-event methods are empty; use Input polling for gameplay.
Resize fits the view to the aspect ratio with vertical half-height 0.9, including
when a custom active camera has been selected.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::GameObject
@ingroup scene
@brief A named transform with owned components and borrowed hierarchy links.
Position and Scale are local values; Rotation is in degrees. Default Scale is
(0.5,0.5). AddComponent owns a component, sets Owner and immediately calls Start.
GetComponent returns the first matching component, or nullptr. Returned pointers
must not be deleted by callers. AddChild maintains hierarchy links and rejects
cycles; it does not transfer ownership or preserve the previous world position.
Both parent and child must still be owned by their scene/application setup.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Component
@ingroup scene
@brief Polymorphic base for behavior attached to a GameObject.
Owner is borrowed. Override Update for logic, Draw for scene rendering and OnGUI
for debug controls. Start runs immediately on attachment, so CurrentScene may
still be null. Destruction is virtual. The default hooks do nothing.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::SpriteRenderer
@ingroup graphics
@brief Draws a quad, triangle or regular polygon using its owner's world matrix.
Retains a shared Material. Quads support texture/UV rectangles; other shapes use
solid tint color. Each renderer has its own UVs, allowing independent animations
with shared materials. PolygonSides defaults to six and drawing clamps it to 3-98.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Material
@ingroup graphics
@brief Shared RGBA appearance and optional shared texture.
TintColor components use the 0-1 range. White preserves texture colors; a material
without a texture draws a solid fill. Editing a shared material affects all its
renderers. Material does not select a custom shader.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Renderer2D
@ingroup graphics
@brief Immediate OpenGL drawing for quads, triangles, polygons and lines.
Application controls Init/Shutdown; Scene controls BeginScene/EndScene. Call draw
functions from a component's Draw hook. Matrix overloads support parent transforms.
Line endpoints are world coordinates. There is no draw batching or layer sorting.
Use Graphics/Renderer2D.h; the old Scene/Renderer2D.h is not the active renderer API.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Texture
@ingroup graphics
@brief Owns an OpenGL RGBA image loaded by stb_image.
Paths use AssetPath. Missing/invalid images throw. Loading uses nearest filtering.
Construct and destroy while the context is alive; share AssetManager handles
rather than copying Texture objects. Bind selects a texture unit for drawing.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Shader
@ingroup graphics
@brief Compiles/links a GLSL program and sets its uniforms.
File/compile/link failures throw and partial allocations are released. Bind before
setting uniforms. The program must be released while its OpenGL context exists.
Application's renderers already manage their default shaders.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::OrthographicCamera
@ingroup graphics
@brief Defines an orthographic view through bounds, position and matrices.
Constructor/SetProjection bounds are left, right, bottom, top. Smaller bounds
show a smaller world area. SetPosition moves the view; X points right, Y up.
Scene resize currently overwrites custom projection bounds.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::ClassicCamera
@ingroup scene
@brief Component that moves the application's active camera to the owner each update.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::SmoothCamera
@ingroup scene
@brief Component that approaches the owner's position using FollowSpeed and delta time.
*/
/**
@struct TigerEngine::SpriteFrame
@ingroup scene
@brief A normalized UV rectangle selecting an atlas frame.
*/
/**
@struct TigerEngine::SpriteAnimation
@ingroup scene
@brief Frame rectangles with a positive frame duration and loop flag.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::SpriteAnimator
@ingroup scene
@brief Advances atlas frames by changing the owner's SpriteRenderer UV rectangle.
Attach SpriteRenderer first. Grid numbers frames from the top-left, row by row.
Clips can loop or stop at the last frame. Stop freezes; Play(name,true) restarts.
Play(name,false) with the same current name does not resume a stopped clip in the
current implementation. GetFrameIndex is relative to the animation clip.
*/
/**
@fn TigerEngine::SpriteAnimation TigerEngine::SpriteAnimator::Grid(int columns, int rows, int firstFrame, int frameCount, float secondsPerFrame, bool loop)
@brief Builds animation rectangles for a regular atlas grid.
@param columns Number of equal-width columns.
@param rows Number of equal-height rows.
@param firstFrame Zero-based start index from the top-left.
@param frameCount Number of consecutive frames to include.
@param secondsPerFrame Duration per frame in seconds.
@param loop Whether playback wraps to the first frame.
@return Animation definition ready for AddAnimation.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::RigidBody2D
@ingroup scene
@brief Optional axis-separated movement with basic box collision resolution.
Call Move explicitly from your controller; gravity is not automatic. The velocity
argument is modified by reference when collision stops motion. Velocity is not
integrated automatically, and HasCollision is currently not checked by Move.
No fixed timestep, rotated-box support or parent-world collision transforms.
OnCollisionEnter is dispatched during vertical overlap resolution and may repeat;
it is not a tracked enter-only event.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::BoxCollider2D
@ingroup scene
@brief Axis-aligned collision box using owner Position/Scale plus Size/Offset.
Size multiplies scale; Offset adds to position. Rotation and parent transforms
are not included. Draw shows a translucent box when Application::ShowHitboxes is true.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::UI
@ingroup ui
@brief ImGui wrapper for debug windows, text, buttons, sliders and checkboxes.
Call from Component::OnGUI and pair BeginWindow with EndWindow. Slider/checkbox
pointers refer to values edited in place. Button returns true on activation.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::UIManager
@ingroup ui
@brief Owns game UI elements and draws them in framebuffer pixels.
Application initializes, updates, draws and shuts it down. Creation methods
return borrowed pointers. SetFont borrows the pointer; keep the owning font handle
alive while UI can draw. Labels do not intercept clicks; panels block UI behind
them. Buttons click on release over the originally pressed button. This does not
automatically consume gameplay Input polling. No child clipping/keyboard navigation.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::UIElement
@ingroup ui
@brief Base for screen-space UI with position, size, visibility and anchors.
Position is an offset from the chosen anchor within the parent or viewport.
Y increases downwards. Parent is borrowed; UIManager owns all elements.
SetParent rejects cycles. Hidden parents hide descendants.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::UILabel
@ingroup ui
@brief Text and color drawn using the UI manager's font.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::UIPanel
@ingroup ui
@brief Solid-color screen-space panel that can parent other UI elements.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::UIButton
@ingroup ui
@brief Text button with color or texture states and optional nine-slice scaling.
Texture handles are retained. SetTextures selects normal/hover/pressed artwork.
Nine-slice borders are source pixels in left/right/top/bottom order. SetOnClick
stores a callback; capture only objects that remain valid until the UI is cleared.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::Font
@ingroup graphics
@brief Owns an ASCII glyph atlas baked from a TrueType font.
Create with an active context. Pixel height defines rasterization size; fonts
cannot be copied or moved. Unsupported bytes render as question marks; this is
not full UTF-8/Polish text support. MeasureText returns nominal layout dimensions;
MeasureVisibleBounds returns visible glyph bounds relative to drawing position.
*/
/**
@class TigerEngine::FontRenderer
@ingroup graphics
@brief Draws text in top-left-origin framebuffer pixels.
Application manages Init/Shutdown. DrawText requires a valid Font and active
context. UI labels and buttons use this renderer internally.
*/
